      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1837, Gooding oversaw construction of the Canal's headquarters building here, and Illinois and Michigan Canal commissioners platted and named the Town of Lockport.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoflockport.net/222/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The headquarters building of the Canal Commission, a National Historic Landmark, today serves as the home of the Illinois and Michigan Canal Museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoflockport.net/222/History",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The arrival of the Chicago and Alton Railroad in 1858 was the catalyst for even more growth in agricultural trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoflockport.net/222/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lockport was incorporated as a town in 1853.",
